---
const { standalone = false } = Astro.props;
---
<section id="saltwater-demo" class="saltwater-lab" aria-labelledby="tank-title">
  <div class="tank-heading"><div><p class="folio-kicker">DENSITY &amp; ROTATION</p>{standalone ? <h1 id="tank-title">Dye &amp; vortices</h1> : <h2 id="tank-title">Dye &amp; vortices</h2>}<p>A denser drop sinks and sets the surrounding water turning. Follow the dye, or choose Vorticity to see the rotation in a cross-section.</p></div><button id="tank-present" type="button">Present the tank ↗</button></div>
  <div class="tank-layout">
    <div class="tank-visual">
      <div class="tank-display" aria-label="Tank display">
        <div class="tank-display-group"><span class="tank-display-label">See the water</span><div class="tank-display-options" role="group" aria-label="Displayed field"><button type="button" data-tank-field="dye" aria-pressed="true">Dye</button><button type="button" data-tank-field="vorticity-z" aria-pressed="false">Vorticity</button><button type="button" data-tank-field="salinity" aria-pressed="false">Salinity</button></div></div>
        <div class="tank-display-group"><span class="tank-display-label">View</span><div class="tank-display-options" role="group" aria-label="Tank geometry"><button type="button" data-tank-geometry="volume" aria-pressed="true">3D tank</button><button type="button" data-tank-geometry="section" aria-pressed="false">Cross-section</button></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="tank-stage">
        <canvas id="dye-tank-canvas" width="1400" height="1050" tabindex="0" aria-label="Three-dimensional water tank. Drag to orbit, scroll or pinch to zoom, tap to release dye, or press Enter for a drop." aria-describedby="tank-instruction"></canvas>
        <div class="tank-corner"><span id="tank-view-label">3D dye</span><output id="tank-clock">0.0 s</output></div>
        <div class="tank-ruler"><span>24 × 18 × 18 cm</span><span>10 °C</span></div>
        <div class="tank-start" id="tank-start" hidden><button id="tank-start-button" type="button">Run the tank ▷</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="tank-stage-key"><p id="tank-reading">Dye shows the path of the released water. Switch to Vorticity to see where the flow turns.</p><div id="tank-legend" class="tank-legend" hidden><span id="tank-legend-low"></span><canvas id="tank-legend-ramp" width="256" height="8" aria-hidden="true"></canvas><span id="tank-legend-high"></span><span id="tank-legend-zero" hidden>0</span></div><p id="tank-vorticity-note" class="tank-caption" hidden></p></div>
      <div class="tank-camera-buttons"><button id="tank-home" type="button">Reset view</button><button id="tank-zoom-in" type="button" aria-label="Zoom into tank">+</button><button id="tank-zoom-out" type="button" aria-label="Zoom out of tank">−</button></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tank-controls">
      <h3 class="tank-controls-heading">Choose an experiment</h3>
      <div class="tank-presets" role="group" aria-label="Tank experiments"><button type="button" data-tank-preset="salt" aria-pressed="true">Salty drop</button><button type="button" data-tank-preset="fresh" aria-pressed="false">Fresh drop</button><button type="button" data-tank-preset="layers" aria-pressed="false">Saline layers</button></div>
      <div class="tank-buttons"><button id="tank-drop-button" type="button">Release dye ↓</button><button id="tank-pause" type="button" aria-pressed="false">Pause</button><button id="tank-reset" type="button">Reset</button></div>
      <fieldset id="tank-layer-editor" class="tank-layer-editor" hidden><legend>Water layers · top to bottom</legend><label>Number of layers<select id="tank-layer-count"><option value="2">Two</option><option value="3" selected>Three</option><option value="4">Four</option></select></label><div id="tank-layer-rows"></div><label>Interface thickness <output id="tank-transition-value">8 mm</output><input id="tank-transition" type="range" min="0" max="30" step="1" value="8"/></label><button id="tank-apply-layers" type="button">Apply layers</button><p id="tank-layer-status" class="tank-caption" role="status">Fresher water above saltier water makes a stable stack.</p></fieldset>
      <h3 class="tank-controls-heading">Set the water and drop</h3>
      <label id="tank-water-label">Water salinity <output id="tank-water-value">30 g/kg</output><input id="tank-water" type="range" min="0" max="40" step="1" value="30"/></label>
      <label>Drop salinity <output id="tank-drop-value">36 g/kg</output><input id="tank-drop" type="range" min="0" max="40" step="1" value="36"/></label>
      <p id="tank-density-meaning" class="tank-meaning">The drop is denser than the water.</p>
      <label>Drop radius <output id="tank-radius-value">22 mm</output><input id="tank-radius" type="range" min="8" max="25" step="1" value="22"/></label>
      <label><span id="tank-plane-label">Release plane</span> <output id="tank-plane-value">9 cm into the tank</output><input id="tank-plane" type="range" min="0" max="100" step="1" value="50"/></label>
      <details class="tank-advanced"><summary>Advanced display</summary><div class="tank-selects"><label>Extra fields<select id="tank-view"><option value="dye">Dye</option><option value="salinity">Salinity</option><option value="speed">Flow speed</option><option value="vorticity">Vorticity strength</option><option value="vorticity-z">Signed vorticity</option></select></label><label>Requested pace<select id="tank-speed"><option value="0.5">½×</option><option value="1" selected>1×</option><option value="2">2×</option></select></label></div><div class="tank-selects"><label>Resolution<select id="tank-quality"><option value="fast">32³ · fast</option><option value="detail" selected>64 × 32 × 32</option><option value="fine">64³ · finer</option></select></label><label>Pointer tool<select id="tank-tool"><option value="orbit">Turn the tank</option><option value="dye">Pour dye</option></select></label></div><label>Cutaway <output id="tank-cutaway-value">Full tank</output><input id="tank-cutaway" type="range" min="20" max="100" step="1" value="100"/></label><label class="tank-check"><input id="tank-flow" type="checkbox"/> Highlight moving water</label><output id="tank-performance" class="tank-caption" aria-live="off">Measuring display and simulation.</output><p class="tank-caption">Display follows the screen’s refresh rate. Finer uses four times as many cells as the middle setting; a larger salinity difference also takes more computation. Requested pace is reached only when the calculation can keep up.</p></details>
      <p id="tank-instruction" class="tank-caption">Drag to turn the tank; scroll or pinch to zoom. Tap to add dye on the release plane. Choose “Pour dye” for continuous drops. Water and resolution changes start a new tank.</p>
      <p id="tank-status" class="tank-caption" role="status">Gold marks a saltier or matching addition; coral marks a fresher one.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="tank-explanation">Dye starts underwater without a push. A density difference drives the water; the dye follows it. In stratified water, a plume can spread sideways near a layer of similar density. Turn the view to see motion through the tank’s full depth.</p>
  <details class="tank-model"><summary>What the physics includes</summary><p>Three-dimensional incompressible Boussinesq flow runs entirely in your browser, with velocity in all three directions. Salt and both pigments use conservative cell-face transfers. Half-step transport before and after the velocity update keeps the density response centered in time. TEOS-10 supplies standard-composition seawater density at 10 °C and atmospheric pressure; the controls use Absolute Salinity in g/kg. Glass sides and bottom resist sliding. The flat top is a rigid lid with zero shear.</p><p>Resolution controls change the actual calculation: 32³, 64 × 32 × 32 or 64³ cells. The finest grid has 3.75 × 2.81 × 2.81 mm cells. Where WebGPU is available, momentum transport uses single precision on the GPU; density, pressure and conservative salt/dye transfers remain in double precision. Other devices use the double-precision reference calculation. Limited transport reduces smearing; it cannot resolve molecular mixing, turbulent entrainment or a drop striking a free surface. Temperature and viscosity are held fixed. The simulated clock can run more slowly on a finer grid or slower device.</p><p>The 3D display traces light through the calculated volume and blends a short queue of computed frames at the screen’s refresh rate. Smooth display motion can continue while the simulated clock runs more slowly. The cross-section samples one physical plane; its slider also places new drops. Cyan and coral show opposite turning directions on that plane, with x right and y down. Drawing resolution adjusts to device performance. WebGL integrates pigment attenuation along the view and light rays to reveal folds and depth. The optical coefficients, colors, lighting and glass are artistic; interpolation adds no physical detail. Salinity uses 0–40 g/kg and flow speed 0–50 mm/s display scales. Vorticity is the curl of the calculated velocity: strength uses 0–8 s⁻¹; signed depth-axis rotation uses −8 to +8 s⁻¹. The signed colors use a square-root stretch to make weaker rotation visible; the endpoints clip. This diagnostic adds no force. Stable-layer, conservation, symmetry, pressure and replay checks accompany grid, timestep and GPU comparisons. <a href="/hidden-rivers/dye-tank/model-coupling.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Time coupling ↗</a> · <a href="/hidden-rivers/dye-tank/model-vorticity.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Vorticity method ↗</a> · <a href="/hidden-rivers/dye-tank/model-3d.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Equations ↗</a> · <a href="/hidden-rivers/dye-tank/verification-3d.json" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Reference results ↗</a> · <a href="/hidden-rivers/dye-tank/model-gpu.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GPU method ↗</a> · <a href="/hidden-rivers/dye-tank/verification-gpu.json" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GPU comparisons ↗</a></p><p><a href="https://www.teos-10.org/pubs/gsw/html/gsw_rho_t_exact.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">TEOS-10 seawater density ↗</a> · <a href="https://www.cs.ubc.ca/~rbridson/fluidsimulation/fluids_notes.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Bridson's fluid simulation notes ↗</a></p></details>
</section>
